FAUX ✓ — soma verify app.cell → ✓ entering Desk.done while Log.armed ; soma run --fresh app.cell ; soma run app.cell Desk.hst x → done ; soma run app.cell Log.gst x → idle. Desk's runtime { } does `emit arm("x")` then moves x to done. The analyses expose runtime { } as a handler of Desk (desugar::expose_for_analysis) and deliver its emit by the one rule — Log, top level, hears it (product.rs:994-1011). The run sends a runtime-section emit (RuntimeEntry::Emit) to Runtime::emit_signal, which reaches Desk's children only (runtime/mod.rs:376-384, 256-268): Log never arms.

Secondary reproducer (app_store.cell): soma run --fresh app.cell ; soma run app.cell Log.n a → 0 (Log.n b → 1). `emit kick("a")` written in Desk's runtime { } reaches Desk's interior only, `go("b")` (a handler of Desk that emits kick) reaches Log too: the "one rule" (Interpreter::hears) is not applied to a runtime-section emit — runtime/mod.rs:376-384 sends RuntimeEntry::Emit to emit_signal (children only); the analyses expose runtime { } as a handler of Desk (desugar::expose_for_analysis) and deliver it to Log.
